    <bpmn:process id="W_W4443" name="W4443. SCO Intervention, Age-Verification &amp; Override Handling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: SCO flag (age/hazmat/controlled/weight/price-override); customer request
Frequency: Continuous (per flagged item)
Volume: Intervention events = flag-rate × SCO volume
Owner: SCO Attendant / Frontend (VS-08) / Compliance (VS-22)
Participants: Attendants, Frontend (VS-08), Compliance (VS-22), DG (VS-114), LP (VS-23), HSE (VS-24)
Source: workflow W4443 — SCO Intervention, Age-Verification &amp; Override Handling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4443_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4443_Lane1" name="Attendant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4443_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4443_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4443_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4443_Lane2" name="Compliance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4443_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4443_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4443_Start4" name="SCO flag (age/hazmat/controlled/weight/price-override); customer request">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4443_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4443_Task5" name="Attendant respond to flag — age-restricted (ID-verify per W4438), DG/hazmat…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Attendant respond to flag — age-restricted (ID-verify per W4438), DG/hazmat (block/authorize per W4438), catch-weight (weigh/measure VS-115), weight-mismatch (re-scan/inspect), price-override (manager auth per SoD)
Responsible (R): Attendant
Accountable (A): Frontend Supervisor / Store Manager
Duration: Per flag</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4443_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4443_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4443_Task6" name="Attendant/Manager authorize override within authority matrix (W4453), log the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Attendant/Manager authorize override within authority matrix (W4453), log the override (exception W4450), and apply the price/quantity change
Responsible (R): Attendant / Manager
Accountable (A): Frontend Supervisor
Duration: Per override</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4443_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4443_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4443_Task7" name="Compliance/LP audit intervention/override patterns for abuse (links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Compliance/LP audit intervention/override patterns for abuse (links W4449/W4450) and tune the flag set (W4438)
Responsible (R): Compliance / LP
Accountable (A): Compliance Lead / LP Lead
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4443_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4443_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4443_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4443_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-92 (ensure self-checkout loss &amp; compliance control.) | - CTL-678: flags actioned per policy; override within authority matrix &amp; logged; age verified; patterns audited (W4449/W4450)
Owner: SCO Attendant / Frontend (VS-08) / Compliance (VS-22)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4443_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4443_Annotation9" targetRef="W4443_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
