    <bpmn:process id="W_W4448" name="W4448. SCO Peak/Queue Management &amp; Host Allocation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Peak (payday/weekend/sale event VS-14); queue buildup
Frequency: Per peak + continuous monitoring
Volume: ~peaks × 200 stores (payday, weekend, sale events, ber-months)
Owner: Frontend Supervisor / Store Ops (VS-07) / WFM (VS-19.3)
Participants: Frontend (VS-08), Store Ops (VS-07), WFM (VS-19.3), LP (VS-23), Customer Safety (VS-147)
Source: workflow W4448 — SCO Peak/Queue Management &amp; Host Allocation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4448_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4448_Lane1" name="Frontend">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4448_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4448_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4448_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4448_Lane2" name="Frontend Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4448_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4448_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4448_Start4" name="Peak (payday/weekend/sale event VS-14); queue buildup">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4448_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4448_Task5" name="Frontend/WFM forecast peak demand, set SCO-pod open ratio &amp; attendant staffing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Frontend/WFM forecast peak demand, set SCO-pod open ratio &amp; attendant staffing, and align to crowd/crowd-safety (VS-147/W4399)
Responsible (R): Frontend / WFM / Store Ops
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per peak</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4448_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4448_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4448_Task6" name="Frontend manage queue in real-time — open/close SCO, allocate attendant…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Frontend manage queue in real-time — open/close SCO, allocate attendant, mobile/line-busting if available, manage intervention queue, and balance vs staffed POS
Responsible (R): Frontend Supervisor / Attendants
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per peak</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4448_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4448_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4448_Task7" name="Frontend/WFM review wait-time/throughput post-peak (W4455), tune…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Frontend/WFM review wait-time/throughput post-peak (W4455), tune staffing/open-ratio, and feed learning to layout (W4435)/WFM (VS-19.3)
Responsible (R): Frontend / WFM / BI
Accountable (A): Store Manager / WFM Lead
Duration: Post-peak</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4448_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4448_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4448_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4448_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-678 (ensure controlled execution — SCO &amp; Scan-&amp;-Go Daily Operations &amp; Customer Experience (PA-149.2).) | - CTL-678: peak forecast &amp; staffing; dynamic open-ratio; intervention queue managed; crowd-safety coordinated (VS-147); post-peak review
Owner: Frontend Supervisor / Store Ops (VS-07) / WFM (VS-19.3)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
